From 1a964d0cf7d25af13ba32db8db47ccd6d148633d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aswin-mcw <aswin.kalies@multicorewareinc.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 01:56:33 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] ARM64: Expect va_hfa to fail on aarch64 Cygwin

The aarch64-pc-cygwin cross GCC (17) passes a 24-byte double HFA to a
variadic function by value in x4-x6, where the Windows ARM64 ABI passes
composites larger than 16 bytes by reference, and its own caller and
callee disagree when an HFA is split between x7 and the stack.  The
smaller HFA cases match libffi.  This is a compiler issue, so mark the
test as an expected failure there.
---
 testsuite/libffi.call/va_hfa.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/testsuite/libffi.call/va_hfa.c b/testsuite/libffi.call/va_hfa.c
index 36f3163..0ac6e8a 100644
--- a/testsuite/libffi.call/va_hfa.c
+++ b/testsuite/libffi.call/va_hfa.c
@@ -6,7 +6,11 @@
    PR:			none.
    Originator:	none.  */
 
-/* { dg-do run } */
+/* The aarch64-pc-cygwin GCC passes variadic HFAs larger than 16 bytes
+   by value and does not agree with itself on HFAs split between x7 and
+   the stack, so it cannot call or implement this function the way the
+   Windows ABI (and MSVC) does.  */
+/* { dg-do run { xfail aarch64*-*-cygwin* aarch64*-*-msys* } } */
 
 #include "ffitest.h"
 #include <stdarg.h>
